wifi: brcmfmac: send action frames that are not P2P, GAS or DPP

brcmf_p2p_send_action_frame() only transmits P2P public action, GAS,
P2P action and DPP frames; for any other action frame it logs "Unknown
Frame" and reports it as not acknowledged without sending it. That
leaves NL80211_CMD_FRAME unusable for every other action frame that
cfg80211 accepts from userspace, for example vendor-specific Public
Action frames (category 4, action 9) that devices exchange without
being in the same BSS, and also the WNM and radio measurement frames
that wpa_supplicant sends to its AP (the "Unknown Frame: category 0xa,
action 0x8" and "category 0x5" messages seen on associated stations).

The firmware's "actframe" iovar sends any action frame, and cfg80211
has already restricted what userspace may send on the interface
(cfg80211_mlme_mgmt_tx()). Send other action frames instead of
dropping them, with the dwell time the caller requested rather than
the P2P default: no P2P exchange follows these frames, and the
firmware answers BCME_BUSY to the next action frame while it is still
dwelling.

Tested on a CYW43455 (firmware 7.45.265, Raspberry Pi 3B+), associated
on channel 1, sending vendor-specific Public Action frames with
NL80211_CMD_FRAME: 100 of 100 unicast frames acknowledged by a peer,
20 of 20 frames to an absent station reported as not acknowledged
(after the driver's retries), and 94 of 100 distinct broadcast frames
received by the peer.

Tool use: this change was prepared with the help of an AI coding
assistant (Claude), which read the driver, wrote the change and the
changelog, and ran the test described in the cover letter; the
submitter reviewed and tested it.

(Upstream series for wireless-next, carried in Splanc's Pi images: pi/provisioning/nix/brcmfmac-actframe.nix.)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
index 37cf6549e..6dd215081 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
@@ -1829,9 +1829,16 @@ bool brcmf_p2p_send_action_frame(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 		/* do not configure anything. it will be */
 		/* sent with a default configuration     */
 	} else {
-		bphy_err(drvr, "Unknown Frame: category 0x%x, action 0x%x\n",
-			 category, action);
-		return false;
+		/* Any other action frame, e.g. a vendor-specific Public Action
+		 * frame: cfg80211 has already checked that it may be sent on
+		 * this interface. No P2P exchange follows it, so dwell only as
+		 * long as the caller asked for; the firmware rejects the next
+		 * action frame while it dwells.
+		 */
+		brcmf_dbg(INFO, "action frame: category 0x%x, action 0x%x\n",
+			  category, action);
+		af_params->dwell_time =
+			cpu_to_le32(requested_dwell & ~CUSTOM_RETRY_MASK);
 	}
 
 	/* if connecting on primary iface, sleep for a while before sending
